#. type: TH
#: original/man1/iostat.1:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "IOSTAT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:6
msgid ""
"iostat - Report Central Processing Unit (CPU) statistics and input/output "
"statistics for devices and partitions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:30
msgid ""
"The B<iostat> command is used for monitoring system input/output device "
"loading by observing the time the devices are active in relation to their "
"average transfer rates. The B<iostat> command generates reports that can be "
"used to change system configuration to better balance the input/output load "
"between physical disks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:47
msgid ""
"The first report generated by the B<iostat> command provides statistics "
"concerning the time since the system was booted, unless the B<-y> option is "
"used (in this case, this first report is omitted).  Each subsequent report "
"covers the time since the previous report. All statistics are reported each "
"time the B<iostat> command is run. The report consists of a CPU header row "
"followed by a row of CPU statistics. On multiprocessor systems, CPU "
"statistics are calculated system-wide as averages among all processors. A "
"device header row is displayed followed by a line of statistics for each "
"device that is configured."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:58
msgid ""
"The I<interval> parameter specifies the amount of time in seconds between "
"each report. The I<count >parameter can be specified in conjunction with the "
"I<interval> parameter. If the I<count >parameter is specified, the value of "
"I<count> determines the number of reports generated at I<interval >seconds "
"apart. If the I<interval >parameter is specified without the I<count "
">parameter, the B<iostat> command generates reports continuously."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: original/man1/iostat.1:59
#, no-wrap
msgid "REPORTS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:64
msgid ""
"The B<iostat> command generates two types of reports, the CPU Utilization "
"report and the Device Utilization report."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:65
#, no-wrap
msgid "CPU Utilization Report"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:71
msgid ""
"The first report generated by the B<iostat> command is the CPU Utilization "
"Report. For multiprocessor systems, the CPU values are global averages among "
"all processors.  The report has the following format:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:72 original/man1/sar.1:1515
#, no-wrap
msgid "%user"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:75 original/man1/mpstat.1:150
msgid ""
"Show the percentage of CPU utilization that occurred while executing at the "
"user level (application)."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:75 original/man1/mpstat.1:150
#: original/man1/sar.1:1523
#, no-wrap
msgid "%nice"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:78 original/man1/mpstat.1:153
msgid ""
"Show the percentage of CPU utilization that occurred while executing at the "
"user level with nice priority."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:78 original/man1/pidstat.1:283
#: original/man1/sar.1:1526
#, no-wrap
msgid "%system"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:81
msgid ""
"Show the percentage of CPU utilization that occurred while executing at the "
"system level (kernel)."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:81 original/man1/mpstat.1:157
#: original/man1/sar.1:1534
#, no-wrap
msgid "%iowait"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:84 original/man1/mpstat.1:160
msgid ""
"Show the percentage of time that the CPU or CPUs were idle during which the "
"system had an outstanding disk I/O request."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:84 original/man1/mpstat.1:164
#: original/man1/sar.1:1537
#, no-wrap
msgid "%steal"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:87 original/man1/mpstat.1:167
msgid ""
"Show the percentage of time spent in involuntary wait by the virtual CPU or "
"CPUs while the hypervisor was servicing another virtual processor."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:87 original/man1/mpstat.1:171
#: original/man1/sar.1:1548
#, no-wrap
msgid "%idle"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:90 original/man1/mpstat.1:174
msgid ""
"Show the percentage of time that the CPU or CPUs were idle and the system "
"did not have an outstanding disk I/O request."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:92
#, no-wrap
msgid "Device Utilization Report"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:113
msgid ""
"The second report generated by the B<iostat> command is the Device "
"Utilization Report.  The device report provides statistics on a per physical "
"device or partition basis. Block devices and partitions for which statistics "
"are to be displayed may be entered on the command line.  If no device nor "
"partition is entered, then statistics are displayed for every device used by "
"the system, and providing that the kernel maintains statistics for it.  If "
"the B<ALL> keyword is given on the command line, then statistics are "
"displayed for every device defined by the system, including those that have "
"never been used.  Transfer rates are shown in 1024-byte blocks by default, "
"unless the environment variable B<POSIXLY_CORRECT> is set, in which case "
"512-byte blocks are used.  The report may show the following fields, "
"depending on the flags used (e.g.  B<-x>, B<-s >and B<-k>, B<-m >or B<-G>):"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:114
#, no-wrap
msgid "Device:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:117
msgid ""
"This column gives the device (or partition) name as listed in the I</dev "
">directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:117 original/man1/sar.1:169 original/man1/sar.1:218
#, no-wrap
msgid "tps"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:122
msgid ""
"Indicate the number of transfers per second that were issued to the "
"device. A transfer is an I/O request to the device. Multiple logical "
"requests can be combined into a single I/O request to the device. A transfer "
"is of indeterminate size."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "Blk_read/s (kB_read/s, MB_read/s, GB_read/s)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:126
msgid ""
"Indicate the amount of data read from the device expressed in a number of "
"blocks (kibibytes, mebibytes, gibibytes) per second. Blocks are equivalent "
"to sectors and therefore have a size of 512 bytes."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:126
#, no-wrap
msgid "Blk_wrtn/s (kB_wrtn/s, MB_wrtn/s, GB_wrtn/s)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:129
msgid ""
"Indicate the amount of data written to the device expressed in a number of "
"blocks (kibibytes, mebibytes, gibibytes) per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:129
#, no-wrap
msgid "Blk_dscd/s (kB_dscd/s, MB_dscd/s, GB_dscd/s)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:132
msgid ""
"Indicate the amount of data discarded for the device expressed in a number "
"of blocks (kibibytes, mebibytes, gibibytes) per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:132
#, no-wrap
msgid "Blk_w+d/s (kB_w+d/s, MB_w+d/s, GB_w+d/s)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:135
msgid ""
"Indicate the amount of data written to or discarded for the device expressed "
"in a number of blocks (kibibytes, mebibytes, gibibytes) per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:135
#, no-wrap
msgid "Blk_read (kB_read, MB_read, GB_read)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:137
msgid "The total number of blocks (kibibytes, mebibytes, gibibytes) read."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:137
#, no-wrap
msgid "Blk_wrtn (kB_wrtn, MB_wrtn, GB_wrtn)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:139
msgid "The total number of blocks (kibibytes, mebibytes, gibibytes) written."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:139
#, no-wrap
msgid "Blk_dscd (kB_dscd, MB_dscd, GB_dscd)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:141
msgid "The total number of blocks (kibibytes, mebibytes, gibibytes) discarded."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:141
#, no-wrap
msgid "Blk_w+d (kB_w+d, MB_w+d, GB_w+d)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:143
msgid ""
"The total number of blocks (kibibytes, mebibytes, gibibytes) written or "
"discarded."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:143 original/man1/tapestat.1:37
#, no-wrap
msgid "r/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:145
msgid ""
"The number (after merges) of read requests completed per second for the "
"device."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:145 original/man1/tapestat.1:39
#, no-wrap
msgid "w/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:147
msgid ""
"The number (after merges) of write requests completed per second for the "
"device."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:147
#, no-wrap
msgid "d/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:149
msgid ""
"The number (after merges) of discard requests completed per second for the "
"device."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:149
#, no-wrap
msgid "f/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:153
msgid ""
"The number (after merges) of flush requests completed per second for the "
"device.  This counts flush requests executed by disks. Flush requests are "
"not tracked for partitions.  Before being merged, flush operations are "
"counted as writes."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:153
#, no-wrap
msgid "sec/s (kB/s, MB/s, GB/s)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:156
msgid ""
"The number of sectors (kibibytes, mebibytes, gibibytes) read from, written "
"to or discarded for the device per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:156
#, no-wrap
msgid "rsec/s (rkB/s, rMB/s, rGB/s)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:158
msgid ""
"The number of sectors (kibibytes, mebibytes, gibibytes) read from the device "
"per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:158
#, no-wrap
msgid "wsec/s (wkB/s, wMB/s, wGB/s)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:160
msgid ""
"The number of sectors (kibibytes, mebibytes, gibibytes) written to the "
"device per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:160
#, no-wrap
msgid "dsec/s (dkB/s, dMB/s, dGB/s)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:162
msgid ""
"The number of sectors (kibibytes, mebibytes, gibibytes) discarded for the "
"device per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:162
#, no-wrap
msgid "rqm/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:164
msgid "The number of I/O requests merged per second that were queued to the device."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:164
#, no-wrap
msgid "rrqm/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:166
msgid ""
"The number of read requests merged per second that were queued to the "
"device."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:166
#, no-wrap
msgid "wrqm/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:168
msgid ""
"The number of write requests merged per second that were queued to the "
"device."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:168
#, no-wrap
msgid "drqm/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:170
msgid ""
"The number of discard requests merged per second that were queued to the "
"device."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:170
#, no-wrap
msgid "%rrqm"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:172
msgid ""
"The percentage of read requests merged together before being sent to the "
"device."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:172
#, no-wrap
msgid "%wrqm"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:174
msgid ""
"The percentage of write requests merged together before being sent to the "
"device."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:174
#, no-wrap
msgid "%drqm"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:176
msgid ""
"The percentage of discard requests merged together before being sent to the "
"device."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:176 original/man1/sar.1:229
#, no-wrap
msgid "areq-sz"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:178 original/man1/sar.1:231
msgid ""
"The average size (in kibibytes) of the I/O requests that were issued to the "
"device."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:180 original/man1/sar.1:233
msgid ""
"Note: In previous versions, this field was known as avgrq-sz and was "
"expressed in sectors."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:180
#, no-wrap
msgid "rareq-sz"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:182
msgid ""
"The average size (in kibibytes) of the read requests that were issued to the "
"device."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:182
#, no-wrap
msgid "wareq-sz"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:184
msgid ""
"The average size (in kibibytes) of the write requests that were issued to "
"the device."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:184
#, no-wrap
msgid "dareq-sz"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:186
msgid ""
"The average size (in kibibytes) of the discard requests that were issued to "
"the device."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:186 original/man1/sar.1:237
#, no-wrap
msgid "await"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:190 original/man1/sar.1:241
msgid ""
"The average time (in milliseconds) for I/O requests issued to the device to "
"be served. This includes the time spent by the requests in queue and the "
"time spent servicing them."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:190
#, no-wrap
msgid "r_await"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:194
msgid ""
"The average time (in milliseconds) for read requests issued to the device to "
"be served. This includes the time spent by the requests in queue and the "
"time spent servicing them."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:194
#, no-wrap
msgid "w_await"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:198
msgid ""
"The average time (in milliseconds) for write requests issued to the device "
"to be served. This includes the time spent by the requests in queue and the "
"time spent servicing them."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:198
#, no-wrap
msgid "d_await"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:202
msgid ""
"The average time (in milliseconds) for discard requests issued to the device "
"to be served. This includes the time spent by the requests in queue and the "
"time spent servicing them."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:202
#, no-wrap
msgid "f_await"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:208
msgid ""
"The average time (in milliseconds) for flush requests issued to the device "
"to be served.  The block layer combines flush requests and executes at most "
"one at a time.  Thus flush operations could be twice as long: Wait for "
"current flush request, then execute it, then wait for the next one."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:208 original/man1/sar.1:233
#, no-wrap
msgid "aqu-sz"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:210 original/man1/sar.1:235
msgid "The average queue length of the requests that were issued to the device."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:212 original/man1/sar.1:237
msgid "Note: In previous versions, this field was known as avgqu-sz."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:212 original/man1/sar.1:241
#, no-wrap
msgid "%util"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:218
msgid ""
"Percentage of elapsed time during which I/O requests were issued to the "
"device (bandwidth utilization for the device). Device saturation occurs when "
"this value is close to 100% for devices serving requests serially.  But for "
"devices serving requests in parallel, such as RAID arrays and modern SSDs, "
"this number does not reflect their performance limits."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:221 original/man1/sadf.1:73
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-c>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:224
msgid "Display the CPU utilization report."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:224
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--compact>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:228
msgid ""
"Don't break the Device Utilization Report into sub-reports so that all the "
"metrics get displayed on a single line."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:228 original/man1/pidstat.1:52
#: original/man1/sadf.1:82 original/man1/sar.1:198
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-d>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:231
msgid "Display the device utilization report."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:239
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-f >I<directory>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:243
msgid "B<+f >I<directory>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:252
msgid ""
"Specify an alternative directory for B<iostat> to read devices "
"statistics. Option B<-f >tells B<iostat >to use only the files located in "
"the alternative directory, whereas option B<+f> tells it to use both the "
"standard kernel files and the files located in the alternative directory to "
"read device statistics."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:255
msgid ""
"I<directory> is a directory containing files with statistics for devices "
"managed in userspace.  It may contain:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:257
msgid ""
"- a \"diskstats\" file whose format is compliant with that located in "
"\"/proc\","
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:260
msgid ""
"- statistics for individual devices contained in files whose format is "
"compliant with that of files located in \"/sys\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:264
msgid ""
"In particular, the following files located in I<directory> may be used by "
"B<iostat>:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:266
msgid "I<directory>/block/I<device>/stat"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:268
msgid "I<directory>/block/I<device>/I<partition>/stat"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:270
msgid ""
"I<partition> files must have an entry in I<directory>/dev/block/ directory, "
"e.g.:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:272
msgid ""
"I<directory>/dev/block/I<major>:I<minor> --E<gt> "
"../../block/I<device>/I<partition>"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:276
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-g >I<group_name >B<{ >I<device >B<[...] | ALL }>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:288
msgid ""
"Display statistics for a group of devices.  The B<iostat> command reports "
"statistics for each individual device in the list then a line of global "
"statistics for the group displayed as I<group_name> and made up of all the "
"devices in the list. The B<ALL> keyword means that all the block devices "
"defined by the system shall be included in the group."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:288 original/man1/mpstat.1:46
#: original/man1/pidstat.1:105 original/man1/sadf.1:129 original/man1/sar.1:326
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-H>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:295
msgid ""
"This option must be used with option B<-g> and indicates that only global "
"statistics for the group are to be displayed, and not statistics for "
"individual devices in the group."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:304
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-j { ID | LABEL | PATH | UUID | ... } [ >I<device >B<[...] | ALL ]>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:315
msgid ""
"Display persistent device names. Keywords B<ID>, B<LABEL>, etc. specify the "
"type of the persistent name. These keywords are not limited, only "
"prerequisite is that directory with required persistent names is present in "
"I</dev/disk>.  Optionally, multiple devices can be specified in the chosen "
"persistent name type.  Because persistent device names are usually long, "
"option B<--pretty> is implicitly set with this option."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:321
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-N>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:325
msgid ""
"Display the registered device mapper names for any device mapper devices.  "
"Useful for viewing LVM2 statistics."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:330
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-p [ { >I<device>B<[,...] | ALL } ]>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:343
msgid ""
"Display statistics for block devices and all their partitions that are used "
"by the system.  If a device name is entered on the command line, then "
"statistics for it and all its partitions are displayed. Last, the B<ALL> "
"keyword indicates that statistics have to be displayed for all the block "
"devices and partitions defined by the system, including those that have "
"never been used. If option B<-j> is defined before this option, devices "
"entered on the command line can be specified with the chosen persistent name "
"type."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:350
msgid ""
"Make the Device Utilization Report easier to read by a human.  The device "
"name will be printed on the right side. The report may also be broken into "
"sub-reports if there are many metrics to display (use B<--compact> option to "
"prevent this)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:350 original/man1/pidstat.1:211
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-s>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:354
msgid ""
"Display a short (narrow) version of the report that should fit in 80 "
"characters wide screens."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:365 original/man1/sadf.1:279 original/man1/sar.1:1588
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-x>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:368
msgid "Display extended statistics."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:372 original/man1/sar.1:1610
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:115
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-z>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:378
msgid ""
"Tell B<iostat> to omit output for any devices for which there was no "
"activity during the sample period."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:383
msgid ""
"The B<iostat> command takes into account the following environment "
"variables:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:383
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<POSIXLY_CORRECT>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:387
msgid ""
"When this variable is set, transfer rates are shown in 512-byte blocks "
"instead of the default 1024-byte blocks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:393 original/man1/mpstat.1:188
#: original/man1/pidstat.1:383 original/man1/sar.1:1626
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:181
msgid ""
"By default statistics are displayed in color when the output is connected to "
"a terminal.  Use this variable to change the settings. Possible values for "
"this variable are I<never>, I<always >or I<auto> (the latter is equivalent "
"to the default settings)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:403 original/man1/mpstat.1:198
#: original/man1/pidstat.1:393 original/man1/tapestat.1:191
msgid ""
"Specify the colors and other attributes used to display statistics on the "
"terminal.  Its value is a colon-separated list of capabilities that defaults "
"to B<I=32;22:N=34;1:W=35;1:X=31;1:Z=34;22>.  Supported capabilities are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:407
msgid "SGR (Select Graphic Rendition) substring for device names."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:410 original/man1/mpstat.1:205
#: original/man1/pidstat.1:400 original/man1/sar.1:1651
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:198
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<W=> (or B<M=>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:414 original/man1/mpstat.1:209
#: original/man1/pidstat.1:404 original/man1/tapestat.1:202
msgid ""
"SGR substring for percentage values in the range from 75% to 90% (or in the "
"range 10% to 25% depending on the metric's meaning)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:414 original/man1/mpstat.1:209
#: original/man1/pidstat.1:404 original/man1/sar.1:1656
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:202
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<X=> (or B<H=>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:418 original/man1/mpstat.1:213
#: original/man1/pidstat.1:408 original/man1/tapestat.1:206
msgid ""
"SGR substring for percentage values greater than or equal to 90% (or lower "
"than or equal to 10% depending on the metric's meaning)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:433
msgid ""
"If this variable exists and its value is B<ISO> then the current locale will "
"be ignored when printing the date in the report header. The B<iostat> "
"command will use the ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD) instead.  The timestamp "
"displayed with option B<-t> will also be compliant with ISO 8601 format."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: original/man1/iostat.1:434 original/man1/mpstat.1:226
#: original/man1/pidstat.1:421 original/man1/sadf.1:355
#: original/man1/sar.1:1697
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXAMPLES"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:435
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<iostat>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:438
msgid "Display a single history since boot report for all CPU and Devices."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:438
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<iostat -d 2>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:441
msgid "Display a continuous device report at two second intervals."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:441
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<iostat -d 2 6>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:444
msgid "Display six reports at two second intervals for all devices."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:444
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<iostat -x sda sdb 2 6>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:448
msgid ""
"Display six reports of extended statistics at two second intervals for "
"devices sda and sdb."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/iostat.1:448
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<iostat -p sda 2 6>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/iostat.1:452
msgid ""
