"The number of IPv6 fragments received per second which needed to be "
"reassembled at this interface [ipv6IfStatsReasmReqds]."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:939
#, no-wrap
msgid "asmok6/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:942
msgid ""
"The number of IPv6 datagrams successfully reassembled per second "
"[ipv6IfStatsReasmOKs]."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:942
#, no-wrap
msgid "imcpck6/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:945
msgid ""
"The number of multicast packets received per second by the interface "
"[ipv6IfStatsInMcastPkts]."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:945
#, no-wrap
msgid "omcpck6/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:948
msgid ""
"The number of multicast packets transmitted per second by the interface "
"[ipv6IfStatsOutMcastPkts]."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:948
#, no-wrap
msgid "fragok6/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:952
msgid ""
"The number of IPv6 datagrams that have been successfully fragmented at this "
"output interface per second [ipv6IfStatsOutFragOKs]."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:952
#, no-wrap
msgid "fragcr6/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:956
msgid ""
"The number of output datagram fragments that have been generated per second "
"as a result of fragmentation at this output interface "
"[ipv6IfStatsOutFragCreates]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:966
msgid ""
"With the B<EIP6> keyword, statistics about IPv6 network errors are "
"reported.  Note that IPv6 statistics depend on B<sadc>'s option B<-S IPV6> "
"to be collected.  The following values are displayed (formal SNMP names "
"between square brackets):"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:967
#, no-wrap
msgid "ihdrer6/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:973
msgid ""
"The number of input datagrams discarded per second due to errors in their "
"IPv6 headers, including version number mismatch, other format errors, hop "
"count exceeded, errors discovered in processing their IPv6 options, "
"etc. [ipv6IfStatsInHdrErrors]"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:973
#, no-wrap
msgid "iadrer6/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:984
msgid ""
"The number of input datagrams discarded per second because the IPv6 address "
"in their IPv6 header's destination field was not a valid address to be "
"received at this entity. This count includes invalid addresses (e.g., ::0) "
"and unsupported addresses (e.g., addresses with unallocated prefixes). For "
"entities which are not IPv6 routers and therefore do not forward datagrams, "
"this counter includes datagrams discarded because the destination address "
"was not a local address [ipv6IfStatsInAddrErrors]."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:984
#, no-wrap
msgid "iukwnp6/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:988
msgid ""
"The number of locally-addressed datagrams received successfully but "
"discarded per second because of an unknown or unsupported protocol "
"[ipv6IfStatsInUnknownProtos]."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:988
#, no-wrap
msgid "i2big6/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:992
msgid ""
"The number of input datagrams that could not be forwarded per second because "
"their size exceeded the link MTU of outgoing interface "
"[ipv6IfStatsInTooBigErrors]."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:992
#, no-wrap
msgid "idisc6/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1000
msgid ""
"The number of input IPv6 datagrams per second for which no problems were "
"encountered to prevent their continued processing, but which were discarded "
"(e.g., for lack of buffer space)  [ipv6IfStatsInDiscards]. Note that this "
"counter does not include any datagrams discarded while awaiting re-assembly."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1000
#, no-wrap
msgid "odisc6/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1009
msgid ""
"The number of output IPv6 datagrams per second for which no problem was "
"encountered to prevent their transmission to their destination, but which "
"were discarded (e.g., for lack of buffer space)  "
"[ipv6IfStatsOutDiscards]. Note that this counter would include datagrams "
"counted in fwddgm6/s if any such packets met this (discretionary) discard "
"criterion."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1009
#, no-wrap
msgid "inort6/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1013
msgid ""
"The number of input datagrams discarded per second because no route could be "
"found to transmit them to their destination [ipv6IfStatsInNoRoutes]."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1013
#, no-wrap
msgid "onort6/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1017
msgid ""
"The number of locally generated IP datagrams discarded per second because no "
"route could be found to transmit them to their destination [unknown formal "
"SNMP name]."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1017
#, no-wrap
msgid "asmf6/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1025
msgid ""
"The number of failures detected per second by the IPv6 re-assembly algorithm "
"(for whatever reason: timed out, errors, etc.) [ipv6IfStatsReasmFails].  "
"Note that this is not necessarily a count of discarded IPv6 fragments since "
"some algorithms can lose track of the number of fragments by combining them "
"as they are received."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1025
#, no-wrap
msgid "fragf6/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1030
msgid ""
"The number of IPv6 datagrams that have been discarded per second because "
"they needed to be fragmented at this output interface but could not be "
"[ipv6IfStatsOutFragFails]."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1030
#, no-wrap
msgid "itrpck6/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1034
msgid ""
"The number of input datagrams discarded per second because datagram frame "
"didn't carry enough data [ipv6IfStatsInTruncatedPkts]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1040
msgid ""
"With the B<NFS> keyword, statistics about NFS client activity are reported.  "
"The following values are displayed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1041
#, no-wrap
msgid "call/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1043
msgid "Number of RPC requests made per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1043
#, no-wrap
msgid "retrans/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1046
msgid ""
"Number of RPC requests per second, those which needed to be retransmitted "
"(for example because of a server timeout)."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1046
#, no-wrap
msgid "read/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1048
msgid "Number of 'read' RPC calls made per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1048
#, no-wrap
msgid "write/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1050
msgid "Number of 'write' RPC calls made per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1050
#, no-wrap
msgid "access/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1052
msgid "Number of 'access' RPC calls made per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1052
#, no-wrap
msgid "getatt/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1054
msgid "Number of 'getattr' RPC calls made per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1060
msgid ""
"With the B<NFSD> keyword, statistics about NFS server activity are "
"reported.  The following values are displayed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1061
#, no-wrap
msgid "scall/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1063
msgid "Number of RPC requests received per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1063
#, no-wrap
msgid "badcall/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1066
msgid ""
"Number of bad RPC requests received per second, those whose processing "
"generated an error."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1066
#, no-wrap
msgid "packet/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1068
msgid "Number of network packets received per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1068
#, no-wrap
msgid "udp/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1070
msgid "Number of UDP packets received per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1070
#, no-wrap
msgid "tcp/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1072
msgid "Number of TCP packets received per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1072
#, no-wrap
msgid "hit/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1074
msgid "Number of reply cache hits per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1074
#, no-wrap
msgid "miss/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1076
msgid "Number of reply cache misses per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1076
#, no-wrap
msgid "sread/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1078
msgid "Number of 'read' RPC calls received per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1078
#, no-wrap
msgid "swrite/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1080
msgid "Number of 'write' RPC calls received per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1080
#, no-wrap
msgid "saccess/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1082
msgid "Number of 'access' RPC calls received per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1082
#, no-wrap
msgid "sgetatt/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1084
msgid "Number of 'getattr' RPC calls received per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1090
msgid ""
"With the B<SOCK> keyword, statistics on sockets in use are reported (IPv4).  "
"The following values are displayed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1091
#, no-wrap
msgid "totsck"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1093
msgid "Total number of sockets used by the system."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1093
#, no-wrap
msgid "tcpsck"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1095
msgid "Number of TCP sockets currently in use."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1095
#, no-wrap
msgid "udpsck"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1097
msgid "Number of UDP sockets currently in use."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1097
#, no-wrap
msgid "rawsck"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1099
msgid "Number of RAW sockets currently in use."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1099
#, no-wrap
msgid "ip-frag"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1101
msgid "Number of IP fragments currently in queue."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1101
#, no-wrap
msgid "tcp-tw"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1103
msgid "Number of TCP sockets in TIME_WAIT state."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1112
msgid ""
"With the B<SOCK6> keyword, statistics on sockets in use are reported "
"(IPv6).  Note that IPv6 statistics depend on B<sadc>'s option B<-S IPV6> to "
"be collected.  The following values are displayed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1113
#, no-wrap
msgid "tcp6sck"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1115
msgid "Number of TCPv6 sockets currently in use."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1115
#, no-wrap
msgid "udp6sck"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1117
msgid "Number of UDPv6 sockets currently in use."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1117
#, no-wrap
msgid "raw6sck"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1119
msgid "Number of RAWv6 sockets currently in use."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1119
#, no-wrap
msgid "ip6-frag"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1121
msgid "Number of IPv6 fragments currently in use."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1127
msgid ""
"With the B<SOFT> keyword, statistics about software-based network processing "
"are reported.  The following values are displayed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1128
#, no-wrap
msgid "total/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1130
msgid "The total number of network frames processed per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1130
#, no-wrap
msgid "dropd/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1133
msgid ""
"The total number of network frames dropped per second because there was no "
"room on the processing queue."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1133
#, no-wrap
msgid "squeezd/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1137
msgid ""
"The number of times the softirq handler function terminated per second "
"because its budget was consumed or the time limit was reached, but more work "
"could have been done."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1137
#, no-wrap
msgid "rx_rps/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1140
msgid ""
"The number of times the CPU has been woken up per second to process packets "
"via an inter-processor interrupt."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1140
#, no-wrap
msgid "flw_lim/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1146
msgid ""
"The number of times the flow limit has been reached per second.  Flow "
"limiting is an optional RPS feature that can be used to limit the number of "
"packets queued to the backlog for each flow to a certain amount.  This can "
"help ensure that smaller flows are processed even though much larger flows "
"are pushing packets in."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1146
#, no-wrap
msgid "blg_len"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1148
msgid "The length of the network backlog."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1158
msgid ""
"With the B<TCP> keyword, statistics about TCPv4 network traffic are "
"reported.  Note that TCPv4 statistics depend on B<sadc>'s option B<-S SNMP> "
"to be collected.  The following values are displayed (formal SNMP names "
"between square brackets):"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1159
#, no-wrap
msgid "active/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1162
msgid ""
"The number of times TCP connections have made a direct transition to the "
"SYN-SENT state from the CLOSED state per second [tcpActiveOpens]."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1162
#, no-wrap
msgid "passive/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1165
msgid ""
"The number of times TCP connections have made a direct transition to the "
"SYN-RCVD state from the LISTEN state per second [tcpPassiveOpens]."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1165
#, no-wrap
msgid "iseg/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1169
msgid ""
"The total number of segments received per second, including those received "
"in error [tcpInSegs].  This count includes segments received on currently "
"established connections."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1169
#, no-wrap
msgid "oseg/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1173
msgid ""
"The total number of segments sent per second, including those on current "
"connections but excluding those containing only retransmitted octets "
"[tcpOutSegs]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1183
msgid ""
"With the B<ETCP> keyword, statistics about TCPv4 network errors are "
"reported.  Note that TCPv4 statistics depend on B<sadc>'s option B<-S SNMP> "
"to be collected.  The following values are displayed (formal SNMP names "
"between square brackets):"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1184
#, no-wrap
msgid "atmptf/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1190
msgid ""
"The number of times per second TCP connections have made a direct transition "
"to the CLOSED state from either the SYN-SENT state or the SYN-RCVD state, "
"plus the number of times per second TCP connections have made a direct "
"transition to the LISTEN state from the SYN-RCVD state [tcpAttemptFails]."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1190
#, no-wrap
msgid "estres/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1194
msgid ""
"The number of times per second TCP connections have made a direct transition "
"to the CLOSED state from either the ESTABLISHED state or the CLOSE-WAIT "
"state [tcpEstabResets]."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1194
#, no-wrap
msgid "retrseg/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1198
msgid ""
"The total number of segments retransmitted per second - that is, the number "
"of TCP segments transmitted containing one or more previously transmitted "
"octets [tcpRetransSegs]."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1198
#, no-wrap
msgid "isegerr/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1201
msgid ""
"The total number of segments received in error (e.g., bad TCP checksums) per "
"second [tcpInErrs]."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1201
#, no-wrap
msgid "orsts/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1203
msgid ""
"The number of TCP segments sent per second containing the RST flag "
"[tcpOutRsts]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1213
msgid ""
"With the B<UDP> keyword, statistics about UDPv4 network traffic are "
"reported.  Note that UDPv4 statistics depend on B<sadc>'s option B<-S SNMP> "
"to be collected.  The following values are displayed (formal SNMP names "
"between square brackets):"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1214
#, no-wrap
msgid "idgm/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1216 original/man1/sar.1:1239
msgid ""
"The total number of UDP datagrams delivered per second to UDP users "
"[udpInDatagrams]."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1216
#, no-wrap
msgid "odgm/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1218 original/man1/sar.1:1242
msgid ""
"The total number of UDP datagrams sent per second from this entity "
"[udpOutDatagrams]."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1218
#, no-wrap
msgid "noport/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1221 original/man1/sar.1:1245
msgid ""
"The total number of received UDP datagrams per second for which there was no "
"application at the destination port [udpNoPorts]."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1221
#, no-wrap
msgid "idgmerr/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1225 original/man1/sar.1:1249
msgid ""
"The number of received UDP datagrams per second that could not be delivered "
"for reasons other than the lack of an application at the destination port "
"[udpInErrors]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1235
msgid ""
"With the B<UDP6> keyword, statistics about UDPv6 network traffic are "
"reported.  Note that UDPv6 statistics depend on B<sadc>'s option B<-S IPV6> "
"to be collected.  The following values are displayed (formal SNMP names "
"between square brackets):"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1236
#, no-wrap
msgid "idgm6/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1239
#, no-wrap
msgid "odgm6/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1242
#, no-wrap
msgid "noport6/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1245
#, no-wrap
msgid "idgmer6/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1255
msgid ""
"The B<ALL> keyword is equivalent to specifying all the keywords above and "
"therefore all the network activities are reported."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1255
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-o [ >I<filename >B<]>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1268
msgid ""
"Save the readings in the file in binary form. Each reading is in a separate "
"record. The default value of the I<filename> parameter is the current "
"standard system activity daily data file. If I<filename> is a directory "
"instead of a plain file then it is considered as the directory where the "
"standard system activity daily data files are located. Option B<-o >is "
"exclusive of option B<-f>.  All the data available from the kernel are saved "
"in the file (in fact, B<sar >calls its data collector B<sadc >with the "
"option B<-S ALL>.  See B<sadc>(8) manual page)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1281
msgid ""
"Report per-processor statistics for the specified processor or processors.  "
"I<cpu_list> is a list of comma-separated values or range of values (e.g., "
"B<0,2,4-7,12->).  Note that processor 0 is the first processor, and "
"processor B<all> is the global average among all processors.  Specifying the "
"B<ALL> keyword reports statistics for each individual processor, and "
"globally for all processors. Offline processors are not displayed."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1281
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-p>, B<--pretty>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1286
msgid ""
"Make reports easier to read by a human.  This option may be especially "
"useful when displaying e.g., network interfaces or block devices statistics."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1286
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-q [ >I<keyword>B<[,...] | ALL ]>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1289
msgid "Report system load and pressure-stall statistics."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1292
msgid "Possible keywords are B<CPU>, B<IO>, B<LOAD>, B<MEM >and B<PSI>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1296
msgid ""
"With the B<CPU> keyword, CPU pressure statistics are reported.  The "
"following values are displayed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1297
#, no-wrap
msgid "%scpu-10"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1300
msgid ""
"Percentage of the time that at least some runnable tasks were delayed "
"because the CPU was unavailable to them, over the last 10 second window."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1300
#, no-wrap
msgid "%scpu-60"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1303
msgid ""
"Percentage of the time that at least some runnable tasks were delayed "
"because the CPU was unavailable to them, over the last 60 second window."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1303
#, no-wrap
msgid "%scpu-300"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1306
msgid ""
"Percentage of the time that at least some runnable tasks were delayed "
"because the CPU was unavailable to them, over the last 300 second window."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1306
#, no-wrap
msgid "%scpu"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1309
msgid ""
"Percentage of the time that at least some runnable tasks were delayed "
"because the CPU was unavailable to them, over the last time interval."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1315
msgid ""
"With the B<IO> keyword, I/O pressure statistics are reported.  The following "
"values are displayed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1316
#, no-wrap
msgid "%sio-10"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1319
msgid ""
"Percentage of the time that at least some tasks lost waiting for I/O, over "
"the last 10 second window."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1319
#, no-wrap
msgid "%sio-60"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1322
msgid ""
"Percentage of the time that at least some tasks lost waiting for I/O, over "
"the last 60 second window."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1322
#, no-wrap
msgid "%sio-300"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1325
msgid ""
"Percentage of the time that at least some tasks lost waiting for I/O, over "
"the last 300 second window."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1325
#, no-wrap
msgid "%sio"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1328
msgid ""
"Percentage of the time that at least some tasks lost waiting for I/O, over "
"the last time interval."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1328
#, no-wrap
msgid "%fio-10"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1331
msgid ""
"Percentage of the time during which all non-idle tasks were stalled waiting "
"for I/O, over the last 10 second window."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1331
#, no-wrap
msgid "%fio-60"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1334
msgid ""
"Percentage of the time during which all non-idle tasks were stalled waiting "
"for I/O, over the last 60 second window."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1334
#, no-wrap
msgid "%fio-300"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1337
msgid ""
"Percentage of the time during which all non-idle tasks were stalled waiting "
"for I/O, over the last 300 second window."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1337
#, no-wrap
msgid "%fio"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1340
msgid ""
"Percentage of the time during which all non-idle tasks were stalled waiting "
"for I/O, over the last time interval."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1346
msgid ""
"With the B<LOAD> keyword, queue length and load averages statistics are "
"reported.  The following values are displayed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1347
#, no-wrap
msgid "runq-sz"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1349
msgid "Run queue length (number of tasks running or waiting for run time)."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1349
#, no-wrap
msgid "plist-sz"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1351
msgid "Number of tasks in the task list."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1351
#, no-wrap
msgid "ldavg-1"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1356
msgid ""
"System load average for the last minute.  The load average is calculated as "
"the average number of runnable or running tasks (R state), and the number of "
"tasks in uninterruptible sleep (D state) over the specified interval."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1356
#, no-wrap
msgid "ldavg-5"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1358
msgid "System load average for the past 5 minutes."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1358
#, no-wrap
msgid "ldavg-15"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1360
msgid "System load average for the past 15 minutes."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1360
#, no-wrap
msgid "blocked"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1362
msgid "Number of tasks currently blocked, waiting for I/O to complete."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1368
msgid ""
"With the B<MEM> keyword, memory pressure statistics are reported.  The "
"following values are displayed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1369
#, no-wrap
msgid "%smem-10"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1372
msgid ""
"Percentage of the time during which at least some tasks were waiting for "
"memory resources, over the last 10 second window."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1372
#, no-wrap
msgid "%smem-60"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1375
msgid ""
"Percentage of the time during which at least some tasks were waiting for "
"memory resources, over the last 60 second window."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1375
#, no-wrap
msgid "%smem-300"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1378
msgid ""
"Percentage of the time during which at least some tasks were waiting for "
"memory resources, over the last 300 second window."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1378
#, no-wrap
msgid "%smem"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1381
msgid ""
"Percentage of the time during which at least some tasks were waiting for "
"memory resources, over the last time interval."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1381
#, no-wrap
msgid "%fmem-10"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1384
msgid ""
"Percentage of the time during which all non-idle tasks were stalled waiting "
"for memory resources, over the last 10 second window."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1384
#, no-wrap
msgid "%fmem-60"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1387
msgid ""
"Percentage of the time during which all non-idle tasks were stalled waiting "
"for memory resources, over the last 60 second window."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1387
#, no-wrap
msgid "%fmem-300"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1390
msgid ""
"Percentage of the time during which all non-idle tasks were stalled waiting "
"for memory resources, over the last 300 second window."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1390
#, no-wrap
msgid "%fmem"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1393
msgid ""
"Percentage of the time during which all non-idle tasks were stalled waiting "
"for memory resources, over the last time interval."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1399
msgid ""
"The B<PSI> keyword is equivalent to specifying CPU, IO and MEM keywords "
"together and therefore all the pressure-stall statistics are reported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1403
msgid ""
"The B<ALL> keyword is equivalent to specifying all the keywords above and "
"therefore all the statistics are reported."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1403
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-r [ ALL ]>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1409
msgid ""
"Report memory utilization statistics. The B<ALL> keyword indicates that all "
"the memory fields should be displayed.  The following values may be "
"displayed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1410
#, no-wrap
msgid "kbmemfree"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1412
msgid "Amount of free memory available in kibibytes."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1412
#, no-wrap
msgid "kbavail"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1421
msgid ""
"Estimate of how much memory in kibibytes is available for starting new "
"applications, without swapping.  The estimate takes into account that the "
"system needs some page cache to function well, and that not all reclaimable "
"slab will be reclaimable, due to items being in use. The impact of those "
"factors will vary from system to system.  If not provided by the kernel, "
"this field is the same as B<kbmemfree>."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1421
#, no-wrap
msgid "kbmemused"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1424
msgid ""
"Amount of used memory in kibibytes (calculated as B<total installed memory> "
"- B<kbavail>)."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1424
#, no-wrap
msgid "%memused"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1426
msgid "Percentage of used memory."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1426
#, no-wrap
msgid "kbbuffers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1428
msgid "Amount of memory used as buffers by the kernel in kibibytes."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1428
#, no-wrap
msgid "kbcached"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1430
msgid "Amount of memory used to cache data by the kernel in kibibytes."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1430
#, no-wrap
msgid "kbcommit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1434
msgid ""
"Amount of memory in kibibytes needed for current workload.  This is an "
"estimate of how much RAM/swap is needed to guarantee that there never is out "
"of memory."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1434
#, no-wrap
msgid "%commit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1438
msgid ""
"Percentage of memory needed for current workload in relation to the total "
"amount of memory (RAM+swap). This number may be greater than 100% because "
"the kernel usually overcommits memory."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1438
#, no-wrap
msgid "kbactive"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1441
msgid ""
"Amount of active memory in kibibytes (memory that has been used more "
"recently and usually not reclaimed unless absolutely necessary)."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1441
#, no-wrap
msgid "kbinact"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1444
msgid ""
"Amount of inactive memory in kibibytes (memory which has been less recently "
"used. It is more eligible to be reclaimed for other purposes)."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1444
#, no-wrap
msgid "kbdirty"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1446
msgid "Amount of memory in kibibytes waiting to get written back to the disk."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1446
#, no-wrap
msgid "kbshmem"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1448
msgid "Amount of shared memory in kibibytes (memory mostly used by tmpfs)."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1448
#, no-wrap
msgid "kbanonpg"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1450
msgid ""
"Amount of non-file backed pages in kibibytes mapped into userspace page "
"tables."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1450
#, no-wrap
msgid "kbslab"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1453
msgid ""
"Amount of memory in kibibytes used by the kernel to cache data structures "
"for its own use."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1453
#, no-wrap
msgid "kbkstack"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1455
msgid "Amount of memory in kibibytes used for kernel stack space."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1455
#, no-wrap
msgid "kbpgtbl"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1457
msgid "Amount of memory in kibibytes dedicated to the lowest level of page tables."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1457
#, no-wrap
msgid "kbvmused"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1459
msgid "Amount of memory in kibibytes of used virtual address space."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1460
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-S>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1464
msgid ""
"Report swap space utilization statistics.  The following values are "
"displayed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1465
#, no-wrap
msgid "kbswpfree"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1467
msgid "Amount of free swap space in kibibytes."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1467
#, no-wrap
msgid "kbswpused"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1469
msgid "Amount of used swap space in kibibytes."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1469
#, no-wrap
msgid "%swpused"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1471
msgid "Percentage of used swap space."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1471
#, no-wrap
msgid "kbswpcad"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1476
msgid ""
"Amount of cached swap memory in kibibytes.  This is memory that once was "
"swapped out, is swapped back in but still also is in the swap area (if "
"memory is needed it doesn't need to be swapped out again because it is "
"already in the swap area. This saves I/O)."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1476
#, no-wrap
msgid "%swpcad"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1478
msgid ""
"Percentage of cached swap memory in relation to the amount of used swap "
"space."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1492
msgid ""
"Set the starting time of the data, causing the B<sar> command to extract "
"records time-tagged at, or following, the time specified. The default "
"starting time is 08:00:00.  Hours must be given in 24-hour format, or as the "
"number of seconds since the epoch (given as a 10 digit number). This option "
"can be used only when data are read from a file (option B<-f>)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1493
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--sadc>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1500
msgid ""
"Indicate which data collector is called by B<sar>.  If the data collector is "
"sought in B<PATH> then enter \"which sadc\" to know where it is located."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1508
msgid ""
"When reading data from a daily data file, indicate that B<sar> should "
"display the timestamps in the original local time of the data file "
"creator. Without this option, the B<sar> command displays the timestamps in "
"the user's local time."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1508
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-u [ ALL ]>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1514
msgid ""
"Report CPU utilization. The B<ALL> keyword indicates that all the CPU fields "
"should be displayed.  The report may show the following fields:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1519
msgid ""
"Percentage of CPU utilization that occurred while executing at the user "
"level (application). Note that this field includes time spent running "
"virtual processors."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1523
msgid ""
"Percentage of CPU utilization that occurred while executing at the user "
"level (application). Note that this field does NOT include time spent "
"running virtual processors."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1526
msgid ""
"Percentage of CPU utilization that occurred while executing at the user "
"level with nice priority."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1530
msgid ""
"Percentage of CPU utilization that occurred while executing at the system "
"level (kernel). Note that this field includes time spent servicing hardware "
"and software interrupts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1534
msgid ""
"Percentage of CPU utilization that occurred while executing at the system "
"level (kernel). Note that this field does NOT include time spent servicing "
"hardware or software interrupts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1537
msgid ""
"Percentage of time that the CPU or CPUs were idle during which the system "
"had an outstanding disk I/O request."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1540
msgid ""
"Percentage of time spent in involuntary wait by the virtual CPU or CPUs "
"while the hypervisor was servicing another virtual processor."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1542
msgid "Percentage of time spent by the CPU or CPUs to service hardware interrupts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1544
msgid "Percentage of time spent by the CPU or CPUs to service software interrupts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1546
msgid "Percentage of time spent by the CPU or CPUs to run a virtual processor."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1548
msgid "Percentage of time spent by the CPU or CPUs to run a niced guest."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1551
msgid ""
"Percentage of time that the CPU or CPUs were idle and the system did not "
"have an outstanding disk I/O request."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1559
msgid ""
"Report status of inode, file and other kernel tables.  The following values "
"are displayed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1560
#, no-wrap
msgid "dentunusd"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1562
msgid "Number of unused cache entries in the directory cache."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1562
#, no-wrap
msgid "file-nr"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1564
msgid "Number of file handles used by the system."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1564
#, no-wrap
msgid "inode-nr"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1566
msgid "Number of inode handlers used by the system."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1566
#, no-wrap
msgid "pty-nr"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1568
msgid "Number of pseudo-terminals used by the system."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1569
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-W>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1572
msgid "Report swapping statistics. The following values are displayed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1573
#, no-wrap
msgid "pswpin/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1575
msgid "Total number of swap pages the system brought in per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1575
#, no-wrap
msgid "pswpout/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1577
msgid "Total number of swap pages the system brought out per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1582
msgid ""
"Report task creation and system switching activity.  The following values "
"are displayed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1583
#, no-wrap
msgid "proc/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1585
msgid "Total number of tasks created per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1587
msgid "Total number of context switches per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1592
msgid ""
"Extended reports: Display minimum and maximum values in addition to average "
"ones at the end of the report."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1595
msgid "Report TTY devices activity. The following values are displayed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1596
#, no-wrap
msgid "rcvin/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1599
msgid ""
"Number of receive interrupts per second for current serial line.  Serial "
"line number is given in the TTY column."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1599
#, no-wrap
msgid "xmtin/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1601
msgid "Number of transmit interrupts per second for current serial line."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1601
#, no-wrap
msgid "framerr/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1603
msgid "Number of frame errors per second for current serial line."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1603
#, no-wrap
msgid "prtyerr/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1605
msgid "Number of parity errors per second for current serial line."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1605
#, no-wrap
msgid "brk/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1607
msgid "Number of breaks per second for current serial line."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1607
#, no-wrap
msgid "ovrun/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1609
msgid "Number of overrun errors per second for current serial line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1615
msgid ""
"Tell B<sar> to omit output for any devices for which there was no activity "
"during the sample period."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1620
msgid "The B<sar> command takes into account the following environment variables:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1635
msgid ""
"Specify the colors and other attributes used to display statistics on the "
"terminal.  Its value is a colon-separated list of capabilities that defaults "
"to B<C=33;22:I=32;22:N=34;1:R=31;22:W=35;1:X=31;1:Z=34;22+=32;1:-=31;1>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1637
msgid "Supported capabilities are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1638
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<C=>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1642
msgid ""
"SGR (Select Graphic Rendition) substring for comments inserted in the binary "
"daily data files."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1645
msgid ""
"SGR substring for item names or values (eg. network interfaces, CPU "
"number...)"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1648
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<R=>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1651
msgid "SGR substring for restart messages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1656
msgid ""
"SGR substring for percentage values in the range from 75% to 90% (or in the "
"range 10% to 25% depending on the metric's meaning).  It is also used for "
"negative values in the range from -10 to -5."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1661
msgid ""
"SGR substring for percentage values greater than or equal to 90% (or lower "
"than or equal to 10% depending on the metric's meaning).  It is also used "
"for negative values lower than or equal to -10."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1664
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<+=>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1667
msgid "SGR substring for battery status (full or charging)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1667
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-=>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1670
msgid "SGR substring for battery status (not charging or discharging)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1671
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<S_REPEAT_HEADER>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1677
msgid ""
"This variable contains the maximum number of lines after which a header has "
"to be displayed by B<sar> when the output is not a terminal."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1688
msgid ""
"If this variable exists and its value is B<UTC >then B<sar> will save its "
"data in UTC time (data will still be displayed in local time).  B<sar> will "
"also use UTC time instead of local time to determine the current daily data "
"file located in the I</var/log/sa> directory. This variable may be useful "
"for servers with users located across several timezones."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1696
msgid ""
"If this variable exists and its value is B<ISO> then the current locale will "
"be ignored when printing the date in the report header.  The B<sar> command "
"will use the ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD) instead.  The timestamp will also "
"be compliant with ISO 8601 format."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1698
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<sar -u 2 5>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1701
msgid "Report CPU utilization for each 2 seconds. 5 lines are displayed."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1701
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<sar -I --int=14 -o int14.file 2 10>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1706
msgid ""
"Report statistics on IRQ 14 for each 2 seconds. 10 lines are displayed.  "
"Data are stored in a file called I<int14.file>."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1706
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<sar -r -n DEV -f /var/log/sa/sa16>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1709
msgid "Display memory and network statistics saved in daily data file I<sa16>."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: original/man1/sar.1:1709
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<sar -A>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1712
msgid "Display all the statistics saved in current daily data file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1716
msgid "I</proc >filesystem must be mounted for the B<sar >command to work."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1720
msgid ""
"All the statistics are not necessarily available, depending on the kernel "
"version used.  B<sar> assumes that you are using at least a 2.6 kernel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1724
msgid ""
"Although B<sar> displays units corresponding to kilobytes (kB), megabytes "
"(MB)..., it actually uses kibibytes (kiB), mebibytes (MiB)...  A kibibyte is "
"equal to 1024 bytes, and a mebibyte is equal to 1024 kibibytes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1736
msgid "I</proc >and I</sys >contain various files with system statistics."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/sar.1:1743
msgid ""
"B<sadc>(8), B<sa1>(8), B<sa2>(8), B<sadf>(1), B<sysstat>(5), B<pidstat>(1), "
"B<mpstat>(1), B<iostat>(1), B<vmstat>(8)"
msgstr ""

#. type: TH
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "TAPESTAT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:6
msgid "tapestat - Report tape statistics."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:10
msgid ""
"B<tapestat [ -k | -m | -G ] [ -t ] [ -U ] [ -V ] [ -y ] [ -z ] [ --human ] [ "
"-o JSON ] [> I<interval >B<[ >I<count >B<] ]>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:14
msgid ""
"The B<tapestat> command is used for monitoring the activity of tape drives "
"connected to a system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:21
msgid ""
"The first report generated by the B<tapestat >command provides statistics "
"concerning the time since the system was booted, unless the B<-y> option is "
"used, when this first report is omitted.  Each subsequent report covers the "
"time since the previous report."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:31
msgid ""
"The I<interval> parameter specifies the amount of time in seconds between "
"each report. The I<count> parameter can be specified in conjunction with the "
"I<interval >parameter. If the I<count >parameter is specified, the value of "
"I<count> determines the number of reports generated at I<interval >seconds "
"apart. If the I<interval >parameter is specified without the I<count> "
"parameter, the B<tapestat> command generates reports continuously."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:37
msgid ""
"The B<tapestat> report provides statistics for each tape drive connected to "
"the system.  The following data are displayed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:39
msgid ""
"The number of reads issued expressed as the number per second averaged over "
"the interval."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:41
msgid ""
"The number of writes issued expressed as the number per second averaged over "
"the interval."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:41
#, no-wrap
msgid "kB_read/s | MB_read/s | GB_read/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:47
msgid ""
"The amount of data read expressed in kibibytes (by default or if option B<-k "
">used), mebibytes (if option B<-m> used) or gibibytes (if option B<-G> used) "
"per second averaged over the interval."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:47
#, no-wrap
msgid "kB_wrtn/s | MB_wrtn/s | GB_wrtn/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:53
msgid ""
"The amount of data written expressed in kibibytes (by default or if option "
"B<-k >used), mebibytes (if option B<-m> used) or gibibytes (if option B<-G> "
"used) per second averaged over the interval."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:53
#, no-wrap
msgid "%Rd"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:58
msgid ""
"Read percentage wait - The percentage of time over the interval spent "
"waiting for read requests to complete.  The time is measured from when the "
"request is dispatched to the SCSI mid-layer until it signals that it "
"completed."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "%Wr"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:62
msgid ""
"Write percentage wait - The percentage of time over the interval spent "
"waiting for write requests to complete. The time is measured from when the "
"request is dispatched to the SCSI mid-layer until it signals that it "
"completed."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "%Oa"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:65
msgid ""
"Overall percentage wait - The percentage of time over the interval spent "
"waiting for any I/O request to complete (read, write, and other)."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:65
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rs/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:68
msgid ""
"The number of I/Os, expressed as the number per second averaged over the "
"interval, where a non-zero residual value was encountered."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ot/s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:74
msgid ""
"The number of I/Os, expressed as the number per second averaged over the "
"interval, that were included as \"other\". Other I/O includes ioctl calls "
"made to the tape driver and implicit operations performed by the tape driver "
"such as rewind on close (for tape devices that implement rewind on "
"close). It does not include any I/O performed using methods outside of the "
"tape driver (e.g. via sg ioctls)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:81
msgid ""
"Show the amount of data written or read in gibibytes per second.  This "
"option is mutually exclusive with B<-k >and B<-m>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:91
msgid ""
"Show the amount of data written or read in kibibytes per second instead of "
"mebibytes.  This option is mutually exclusive with B<-G >and B<-m>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:96
msgid ""
"Show the amount of data written or read in mebibytes per second instead of "
"kibibytes.  This option is mutually exclusive with B<-G >and B<-k>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:106
msgid ""
"Display time stamps. The time stamp format may depend on the value of the "
"B<S_TIME_FORMAT >environment variable (see below) and on whether option -U "
"has been used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:112
msgid "Print version and exit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:115
msgid "Omit the initial statistic showing values since boot."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:120
msgid ""
"Tell B<tapestat> to omit output for any tapes for which there was no "
"activity during the sample period."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:121
#, no-wrap
msgid "CONSIDERATIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:128
msgid ""
"It is possible for a percentage value (read, write, or other) to be greater "
"than 100 percent (the B<tapestat> command will never show a percentage value "
"more than 999).  If rewinding a tape takes 40 seconds where the interval "
"time is 5 seconds the %Oa value would show as 0 in the intervals before the "
"rewind completed and then show as approximately 800 percent when the rewind "
"completes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:134
msgid ""
"Similar values will be observed for %Rd and %Wr if a tape drive stops "
"reading or writing and then restarts (that is it stopped streaming). In such "
"a case you may see the r/s or w/s drop to zero and the %Rd/%Wr value could "
"be higher than 100 when reading or writing continues (depending on how long "
"it takes to restart writing or reading).  This is only an issue if it "
"happens a lot as it may cause tape wear and will impact on the backup times."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:141
msgid ""
"For fast tape drives you may see low percentage wait times.  This does not "
"indicate an issue with the tape drive. For a slower tape drive (e.g. an "
"older generation DDS drive) the speed of the tape (and tape drive) is much "
"slower than filesystem I/O, percent wait times are likely to be higher. For "
"faster tape drives (e.g. LTO) the percentage wait times are likely to be "
"lower as program writing to or reading from tape is going to be doing a lot "
"more filesystem I/O because of the higher throughput."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:148
msgid ""
"Although tape statistics are implemented in the kernel using atomic "
"variables they cannot be read atomically as a group. All of the statistics "
"values are read from different files under I</sys>, because of this there "
"may be I/O completions while reading the different files for the one tape "
"drive. This may result in a set of statistics for a device that contain some "
"values before an I/O completed and some after."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:158
msgid ""
"This command uses rounding down as the rounding method when calculating per "
"second statistics.  If, for example, you are using B<dd >to copy one tape to "
"another and running B<tapestat> with an interval of 5 seconds and over the "
"interval there were 3210 writes and 3209 reads then w/s would show 642 and "
"r/s 641 (641.8 rounded down to 641). In such a case if it was a tar archive "
"being copied (with a 10k block size) you would also see a difference between "
"the kB_read/s and kB_wrtn/s of 2 (one I/O 10k in size divided by the "
"interval period of 5 seconds). If instead there were 3210 writes and 3211 "
"reads both w/s and r/s would both show 642 but you would still see a "
"difference between the kB_read/s and kB_wrtn/s values of 2 kB/s."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:169
msgid ""
"This command is provided with an interval in seconds. However internally the "
"interval is tracked per device and can potentially have an effect on the per "
"second statistics reported.  The time each set of statistics is captured is "
"kept with those statistics. The difference between the current and previous "
"time is converted to milliseconds for use in calculations.  We can look at "
"how this can impact the statistics reported if we use an example of a tar "
"archive being copied between two tape drives using B<dd>.  If both devices "
"reported 28900 kibibytes transferred and the reading tape drive had an "
"interval of 5001 milliseconds and the writing tape drive 5000 milliseconds "
"that would calculate out as 5778 kB_read/s and 5780 kB_wrtn/s."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:171
msgid ""
"The impact of some retrieving statistics during an I/O completion, rounding "
"down, and small differences in the interval period on the statistics "
"calculated should be minimal but may be non-zero."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:175
msgid ""
"The B<tapestat> command takes into account the following environment "
"variables:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:195
msgid "SGR (Select Graphic Rendition) substring for tape names."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:221
msgid ""
"If this variable exists and its value is B<ISO> then the current locale will "
"be ignored when printing the date in the report header. The B<tapestat> "
"command will use the ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD) instead.  The timestamp "
"displayed with option B<-t> will also be compliant with ISO 8601 format."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:226
msgid ""
"I</sys >filesystem must be mounted for B<tapestat> to work. It will not work "
"on kernels that do not have sysfs support"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:229
msgid ""
"This command requires kernel version 4.2 or later (or tape statistics "
"support backported for an earlier kernel version)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: original/man1/tapestat.1:233
msgid ""
"Although B<tapestat> displays units corresponding to kilobytes (kB), "
"megabytes (MB), gigabytes (GB)..., it actually uses kibibytes (kiB), "
"mebibytes (MiB), gibibytes (GiB)...  A kibibyte is equal to 1024 bytes, a "
"mebibyte is equal to 1024 kibibytes, and a gibibyte is equal to 1024 "
"mebibytes."
msgstr ""

